   "text": {
    "L1": "Meenu wants to learn, but she is kept at home while her brothers do homework.",
    "L2": "She feels left out and sad, so she asks the river, “Why can't I go to school too?”",
    "L3": "Here is a myth: putting Why before a statement makes a correct question.",
    "L4": "Not true. In a question, Why comes first, then the helper does, then the subject.",
    "L5": "Because does already carries the -s, the main verb stays in its base form: stay.",
    "L6": "So we say, “Why does Meenu stay at home?” The question leads her to speak to the headmaster.",
    "L7": "The message is clear: asking questions and speaking up is how learning starts, and every child has a right to learn.",
    "L8": "Now choose the word order for a correct Why question."
   },
